{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke, etc.: נָשֹׂא.</b> It was necessary to say <b>וַיְדַבֵּר</b> a second time, and it would not have sufficed with what He said, ״וַיְדַבֵּר ה׳,״ at the counting of the sons of Kehath earlier in the portion of בַּמִּדְבַּר, because He comes to state a different matter besides the counting, namely that He would lift up and elevate the sons of Gershon in comparison to the sons of Merari. And this matter is a thing in itself, for this lifting is not in the category of the lifting of the sons of Kehath, who bear the Ark — therefore He established for it a separate utterance. And for this reason, when He commanded regarding the counting of the sons of Merari, He said ״בְּנֵי מְרָרִי etc. תִּפְקֹד״ — He did not establish for them a separate utterance, for they have no distinction other than a number, in that He said ״תִּפְקֹד״ and not ״תִּשָּׂא.״" "<b>Unto Moses, etc.</b> And further on, in the counting, it says <b>וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן</b> (Numbers 4:34), because there the command comes to Aaron in order that he arrange the order stated regarding the burden of the sons of Kehath, as it is written ״וְשָׂמוּ אוֹתָם etc. וְלֹא יָמֻתוּ״ — therefore it says <b>וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן</b>, which is not needed for the burden of the sons of Gershon."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:05.042602453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}